1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,000
AI agents will consume millions of APIs.

2
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:14,000
They can't discover them. Can't read them. Can't pay for them.

3
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:22,000
Tollbooth is the missing commerce layer for the machine economy.

4
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:30,000
A developer pastes an OpenAPI spec…

5
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:40,000
…and gets an SDK plus an agent-readable context file — docs machines can read.

6
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:48,000
The listing goes live with per-call pricing.

7
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:56,000
Now the demand side. An AI agent gets a mission:

8
00:00:56,000 --> 00:01:04,000
"Find a sentiment API. Run 3 calls. Stay under $5."

9
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:12,000
It searches the marketplace via MCP…

10
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:20,000
…reads the context file…

11
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:30,000
…creates a $5 PayPal order for 500 credits.

12
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:38,000
PayPal captures the payment — no browser, no human.

13
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:46,000
Credits land instantly.

14
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:56,000
Every call is metered: 2¢ each. Failed calls are never billed.

15
00:01:56,000 --> 00:02:06,000
The developer watches revenue and usage update live.

16
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:14,000
Earnings pay out to the seller's PayPal account.

17
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:22,000
Zero humans touched this transaction.

18
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:34,000
Every API, ready for the machine economy.

19
00:02:34,000 --> 00:02:50,000
Tollbooth — github.com/adelekevictor12/tollbooth
